#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096502 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96967f25-565a-5338-878e-00fd30055772" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area Bounded Below a Curve and Above the X-Axis"}] :question/id #uuid "dc29cf6e-4f68-552e-ae7a-f9834eec1bd7" :question/math-academy-id "e-781" :question/problem "Find the area between the curve $y=x^2-2x+2,$ the $x$-axis, and the lines $x=0$ and $x=2.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/assets/6b85f10cde49017eac1c56ad1b8abbcdf3033a367d5e1eb162dd89fbb6141461.png)" :question/worked-solution "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}({x}^{2}-2x+2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-2{\\int }_{0}^{2}x\\,\\text{d}x+2{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}|}_{0}^{2}-2\\cdot {\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}|}_{0}^{2}+2x{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{8}{3}-0)-2(2-0)+2(2-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}-4+4 \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096503 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6ad216da-1bcf-5b87-9436-918ef1e5015a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area Bounded Above a Curve and Below the X-Axis"}] :question/id #uuid "5893a692-573a-5e1a-81aa-db34fa6059ed" :question/math-academy-id "e-782" :question/problem "Find the area of the closed region between the curve $y=x^2-1$ and the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the intersections of the curve with the $x$-axis:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-1 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =1 \\\\ x & =\\pm 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe draw a sketch of the region, as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/assets/9b78aad41f84f6a6997914bd8d4243f30cb0ebea4edb5305962dc11c7a46a807.png)\n\nWe want the area between the curve $y=x^2-1$ and the $x$-axis, from $x=-1$ to $x=1.$ To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}({x}^{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}|}_{-1}^{1}-x{|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{3}-(-\\frac{1}{3}))-(1-(-1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}-2 \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is $\\dfrac{4}{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186286979 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6ad216da-1bcf-5b87-9436-918ef1e5015a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area Bounded Above a Curve and Below the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02d2d42c-a2f6-5794-98d1-e9f45e363f20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286981} {:answer/id #uuid "8aaa62df-b3d3-5788-932b-ac74df33f711" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286982} {:answer/id #uuid "6c04dcf5-bb0e-519d-bea6-29b3eaafd011" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286983} {:answer/id #uuid "8a2f18ac-79ee-5da0-af4b-3b111f5d3115" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286984} {:answer/id #uuid "edb5b488-bf49-5b1d-877c-a110c0b28fc5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286985}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8aaa62df-b3d3-5788-932b-ac74df33f711" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286982} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d637e68-da4f-5b6c-a95a-d87f9ad2692b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286980}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0c21d4e0-baa2-59e6-b265-1bfdd4a8ba84" :question/math-academy-id "q-103824" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/assets/97cf633bce7a8eeef443757e62d52f356c911b6aee3d8019d434d514416b0049.png)\n\nA region is bounded by the curve $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and the $x$-axis between $x=-\\pi $ and $x=0$, as shown above. What is the area of the region?" :question/worked-solution "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{0}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x{|}_{-\\pi }^{0} \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)-(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\pi )) \\\\  & =-1-(1) \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is $2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186286986 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96967f25-565a-5338-878e-00fd30055772" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area Bounded Below a Curve and Above the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88921aa9-5ce7-5e3e-aa94-34c52a208bc4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{27}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286988} {:answer/id #uuid "6e53459d-c26f-581f-b92e-5cfdc3e630c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286989} {:answer/id #uuid "fb09bab5-1f31-56c1-8aaf-5580ef2ace97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{19}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286990} {:answer/id #uuid "202ffa58-272b-5ce4-9590-e7cb3244049f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{19}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286991} {:answer/id #uuid "6d8539f1-4620-5fe3-bbb0-2ccce10dc720" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286992}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e53459d-c26f-581f-b92e-5cfdc3e630c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286989} :answer-field/id #uuid "bac6f17e-69ff-50d1-82e1-0fbc84fa2799" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286987}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "14aae701-3d97-58e0-b9cc-218ca30f5a80" :question/math-academy-id "q-10978" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/assets/09482b1e9903bff25b16b2239975831e6d54440a8f8ea78f5739b0eafee3d9e8.png)\n\nFind the area between the curve $y=-2{x}^{2}-x+3$, the $x$-axis and the $y$-axis, shown above." :question/worked-solution "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(-2{x}^{2}-x+3)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-1{\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\,\\text{d}x+3{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2\\cdot {\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}|}_{0}^{1}-1\\cdot {\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}|}_{0}^{1}+3x{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-2(\\frac{1}{3}-0)-1(\\frac{1}{2}-0)+3(1-0) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{1}{2}+3 \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186286993 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96967f25-565a-5338-878e-00fd30055772" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area Bounded Below a Curve and Above the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7ad04aee-4354-5499-a9c4-5d32782153cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt{3}+\\ln(2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286995}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7ad04aee-4354-5499-a9c4-5d32782153cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt{3}+\\ln(2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286995} :answer-field/id #uuid "cfbc56d0-6cf5-56e8-832a-e1f5ce426489" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286994}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "3dc8a6c1-7592-5eeb-a313-53d3c7edaf54" :question/math-academy-id "q-316022" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/assets/b5432ed129d85a3718f8e5ebe0cca141731c366d1b32e8e72d0916c60c34de2c.png)\n\nA region in the $x$-$y$ plane is bounded by the curve $y={sec}^{2}⁡x+\\frac{1}{x}$, and the $x$-axis between $x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ and $x=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$, as shown above. \nFind the area $A$ of the region. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}({sec}^{2}⁡(x)+\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}{sec}^{2}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,+\\,{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)){|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{3}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{3})-(\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{\\pi /3}{\\pi /6} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186286996 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6ad216da-1bcf-5b87-9436-918ef1e5015a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area Bounded Above a Curve and Below the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f8087994-f633-5222-bc42-b0ed8f245d96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286998}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f8087994-f633-5222-bc42-b0ed8f245d96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286998} :answer-field/id #uuid "711f7b04-3786-56a4-83fc-600b47fb0b3d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286997}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0898c71c-a5cb-5f15-ba0d-a57bf7aea007" :question/math-academy-id "q-316024" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/assets/d282e4afd0a66dd79fecf474da9f618a5970197943044d24208f86c4c43781e6.png)\n\nA region is bounded by the curve $y=-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}$, the $x$-axis, and the lines $x=-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ and $x=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$, as shown above. Find the area $A$ of the region. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-\\sqrt{2}/2}^{\\sqrt{2}/2}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{2}/2}^{\\sqrt{2}/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x{|}_{-\\sqrt{2}/2}^{\\sqrt{2}/2} \\\\  & =-(arcsin\\,(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})-arcsin\\,(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{4}+(-\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is \n\n$$\nA=-{\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186286999 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96967f25-565a-5338-878e-00fd30055772" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area Bounded Below a Curve and Above the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e57ad0b-9483-526c-890b-8610e0c25573" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287001}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e57ad0b-9483-526c-890b-8610e0c25573" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287001} :answer-field/id #uuid "02cd5950-75bb-531f-baa4-a242087bb56b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287000}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "af0957a3-156c-55af-b348-c5c2666a8fa7" :question/math-academy-id "q-345319" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/assets/0a4b4be4f7de918b847245372077e159f60f3834bb37ef00f4873e63b4cea894.png)\n\nA region is bounded by the curve $y={e}^{x}$ and the $x$-axis between $x=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)$ and $x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)$, as shown above. Find the area $A$ of the region. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{x}{|}_{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}-{e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)} \\\\  & =2-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287002 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96967f25-565a-5338-878e-00fd30055772" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area Bounded Below a Curve and Above the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f2234af5-c4b4-528e-a73d-9112c3bcf211" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287004} {:answer/id #uuid "dd04ae4e-8b2a-583a-99ac-cefd48c3c441" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287005}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dd04ae4e-8b2a-583a-99ac-cefd48c3c441" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287005} :answer-field/id #uuid "3a308356-6fe7-5b58-823a-c078c0fdfb17" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287003}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7dc244c3-54c6-5170-b8f9-917b4e9e083b" :question/math-academy-id "q-345322" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/assets/66bf8c1144de1ad65938345d2937fddd6fb43ec4822a2b98a9b5383ca2609567.png)\n\nA region is bounded by the curve $y=-2{x}^{2}+3$ and the $x$-axis between $x=0$ and $x=1$, as shown above. Find the area $A$ of the region. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(-2{x}^{2}+3)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(-2\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+3x){|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(-\\frac{2}{3}+3)-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287006 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6ad216da-1bcf-5b87-9436-918ef1e5015a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area Bounded Above a Curve and Below the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e1f9a6a-e10b-58a2-a01b-182ae2eeed8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287008}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e1f9a6a-e10b-58a2-a01b-182ae2eeed8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287008} :answer-field/id #uuid "8715be83-ce41-55ca-9341-52a474fd23f8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287007}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "10fa10cd-fc6f-507a-99f5-6fa17f1da5d9" :question/math-academy-id "q-345343" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/assets/34eb73b6bd93f9a45b666ed0599719a09b54948d1d81b14ceea9b46f99b75054.png)\n\nFind the area between the curve $y=-{x}^{2}-1$, the $x$-axis, and the line $x=-1$ and $x=1$ (shown above). Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}(-{x}^{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}|}_{-1}^{1}-x{|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =-(\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{(-1)^{3}}{3})-(1-(-1)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}-2 \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is \n\n$$\nA=-{\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{8}{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287009 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6ad216da-1bcf-5b87-9436-918ef1e5015a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area Bounded Above a Curve and Below the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aa3dc2fa-4986-554c-83a6-9a6de5d5401f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287011} {:answer/id #uuid "6747e758-6554-57f1-a112-5e4fcdd611c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287012}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6747e758-6554-57f1-a112-5e4fcdd611c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287012} :answer-field/id #uuid "55f5b3e8-bdcb-5dee-90c0-d3879f2619f3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287010}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "79d1f903-1ab4-5a5d-94d4-eace512d810a" :question/math-academy-id "q-345381" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/assets/dce89dbea62566c0ee897bffe0638458970799bafdc7d7c8e5084328fef38bef.png)\n\nA region is bounded by the curve $y=-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}$, the $x$-axis, and the lines $x=-1$ and $x=1$, as shown above. Find the area $A$ of the region. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-arcsin\\,(\\frac{x}{2}){|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =-(arcsin\\,(\\frac{1}{2})-arcsin\\,(-\\frac{1}{2})) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+(-\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is \n\n$$\nA=-{\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{\\pi }{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287013 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96967f25-565a-5338-878e-00fd30055772" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area Bounded Below a Curve and Above the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d12a0620-00d1-5952-a69e-06e1a9ba761b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287015} {:answer/id #uuid "c381f770-778e-5ccd-993b-3797afeba2a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287016} {:answer/id #uuid "c057d538-1733-5266-b831-f8d63c0eb129" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt[3]{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287017} {:answer/id #uuid "d6c226fd-3c8d-58cc-b2e6-6f70d51d8e1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287018} {:answer/id #uuid "01063069-e246-5f12-b01d-b72666e18038" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287019}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "01063069-e246-5f12-b01d-b72666e18038" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287019} :answer-field/id #uuid "555f6e53-800c-5247-a583-8629aac2480f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287014}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "14752328-fec5-5213-a8b6-ccc1fe3ce177" :question/math-academy-id "q-54474" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/assets/de15e1e9433a3560cbc8268904f4f62fbbb721c3b5b9a700c59fea0941829406.png)\n\nThe area of the shaded region between the curve $y={x}^{3}+8$ and the $x$-axis is given by the integral expression below. What is the value of $a?$\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{a}^{2}({x}^{3}+8)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To get $a$, we need to find the $x$-intercepts of the curve $y={x}^{3}+8.$ \n\nWe solve the equation for $y=0$: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}+8 & =y \\\\ {x}^{3}+8 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{3} & =-8 \\\\ x & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=-2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287020 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6ad216da-1bcf-5b87-9436-918ef1e5015a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area Bounded Above a Curve and Below the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f112e36-2d53-59a1-b16a-8f9b49ca15e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287022} {:answer/id #uuid "ee8ada9f-2cfa-5d32-80d7-fcb52fe23c08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287023} {:answer/id #uuid "cb61c6c0-438a-53fc-8c13-638c6b8a9846" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287024} {:answer/id #uuid "317e331e-877c-5961-8298-0690cd98a699" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287025} {:answer/id #uuid "9a75289d-0f98-54fe-aaf7-8b1c9899a80f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287026}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "317e331e-877c-5961-8298-0690cd98a699" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287025} :answer-field/id #uuid "1c15c80e-3510-55b8-9353-1985f3adce45" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287021}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "61cc7b90-6261-5d84-a76c-eb58b2277a06" :question/math-academy-id "q-73333" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/assets/1819bad0219f1709a01100daad00beb25a8bbc3688f9fe7c41be53bad8010455.png)\n\nA region is bounded by the curve $y=-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}$, the $x$-axis, and the lines $x=-0.5$ and $x=0.5$, as shown above. What is the area of the region?" :question/worked-solution "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-0.5}^{0.5}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{-0.5}^{0.5}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x{|}_{-0.5}^{0.5} \\\\  & =-(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(0.5)-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-0.5)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+(-\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is $\\frac{\\pi }{3}.$"}]}
